# Paper Metadata Extraction and Catalog Resolution Plan

Last updated: 2026-07-29

## Objective

Build a two-stage asynchronous paper-information pipeline:

1. Python extracts candidate title, authors, abstract, and raw references from
   persisted Markdown and source-map blocks.
2. Go queries paper catalogs such as Semantic Scholar, OpenAlex, arXiv, and
   Crossref, ranks normalized candidates, and safely updates canonical
   `paper_metadata`.

Document recognition must remain independent: paper-information failure must not
change a successfully parsed document from `ready` to `failed`.

